  "prefLabel": "Odb 402.17 Other insurance",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Odb 402.17 “Other insurance” means private insurance coverage for corrective action or third-party damage costs that is valid and collectible by the owner, and includes private insurance held by the owner through either a wholly-owned or jointly-owned subsidiary in the business of providing insurance coverage to the owner or to the owner and others.\n\nSource. #12942, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/odb100-600.html"
